A||||9||Raiden||What's The Diff?||||1||
Z||000000||Raiden||09-04-2001||03:34 AM||||I was just wondering what the difference between the V6 4speed and 5speed..<BR>Is there more power in the 4? <BR>Or Is the 5 just more econommical?<BR>what's the deal?<BR>I Need Your Help!!!<P>*i want to learn* =D||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-04-2001||04:09 AM||||I have the gear ratios somewhere...I think the 5 speeds have more of an overdrive.<P>I love my 4 speed!  Especially with taller tires, 1st gear is actually useful.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif"> <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-04-2001||10:55 PM||||same, in theroey, as the difference between a 5-speed and a 6-speed.  Tighter gear spacing.<P>It's a preference thing, I couldn't imagine driving a 4-speed car, but some people seem to like them.<P>My best advice as to how they apply in a Fiero is; go drive both  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||fiero56||09-04-2001||11:02 PM||||I love the stock 4-speed mated to my v-6. 4-speed has 3.65 f/d, Getrag has 3.61. My getrag is useless in 1st, and gear spacing seems disorganized. My 4-speed has usefull gears, they are spaced very well, and it shifts smoother than my Getrag. 65mph with the 4-speed is 2,500rpm, I think my Getrag at 65mph spins teh engine at 2,200. Its been a while since I've compared so my rpms may be off.||||reg||1
Z||000004||banditbalz||09-04-2001||11:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raiden:<BR><B><BR>Is there more power in the 4? <BR>Or Is the 5 just more econommical?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The 4 speed Muncie has longer gear ratios than the 5 speed Getrag. The 173lb.ft. of torque allows quicker acceleration in the 4 speed.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||09-04-2001||11:12 PM||||The ONLY thing I have against the 4-speeds is where they put reverse.  Would it have killed them to have reverse down and to the right (like the 5-speeds)?  <P>There is nothing worse, to me, than pushing the lever to the right then up.....it's just annoying.<P>Some people hate the Getrag, but love the 4-speed and vice versa......I think the main issue is with the mileage and abuse that a <BR>particular tranny has seen.  I have driven new Fieros (I just sold a 5-sp. Formula w/less than 300 miles) and the trannies shifted as smooth as silk.  However, Getrags tend to get notchier as they age, so a lower mileage 4-sp. will feel better to some who have driven high mileage/notchy Getrags.<P>The same thing can be said about the 4-speeds.....I personally like the 5-sp. over the 4 sp., but that's just my opinion.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cheever3000||09-04-2001||11:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>quicker acceleration in the 4 speed.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Sounds like a challenge to me.<BR>I'll take on any stock 2.8 w/4-spd against my stock 2.8 '88 w/5-spd!<P>That doesn't mean I'll <I>win</I>, but I'll take em on.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||09-04-2001||11:27 PM||||For fun in the city, screwing around, the 4-speed is my favorite. Shifts are spread out, and don't come as fast or as often. I prefer my Getrag for cruising or highway use.<P>I agree, my Getrag is a high-mileage unit, and my Muncie is lower mileage. I also hate the left-and-up for reverse. <P>If my Getrag were smooth shifting, I'm sure I would like it much more. I'm planning on having lower mileage pieces installed soon, so I won't have to fuss about it much longer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Cheever:<BR>I've got a pretty fast stock 2.8 with 4-speed mated to it. One of, if not THE strongest pulling, 2.8s I've driven. My Getrag has the weakest pulling 2.8L I've driven. Another reason I may not prefer my Getrag car, but in a couple more weeks this will all change <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||banditbalz||09-04-2001||11:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B><BR>I'll take on any stock 2.8 w/4-spd against my stock 2.8 '88 w/5-spd!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cheever, I have raced many stock 5 speeds. On track and off track, iv'e never lost to one yet... too bad Texas wasn't a little closer to CANADA!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/HardLaunch_4.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000009||Leadfoot||09-04-2001||11:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>The ONLY thing I have against the 4-speeds is where they put reverse.  Would it have killed them to have reverse down and to the right (like the 5-speeds)?  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No kidding, I almost backed into a cop at the lights on day as I fumbled to find 1st.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> He followed me for a couple of miles until he turned around.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
